  "full_text": "Okay, this is my operating system and I made a new game. I call it Chessnet. The board is mirrored and it's random. It's kind of like, well, a little bit like checkers, I guess. But the idea is these are networks that I was thinking of like computer networks. And you try to break the network links. So the way it goes is you try to capture the king, break his networks. You step on the midpoint to kill it. So this guy tries to step on his midpoint, but he can't reach. It's kind of tricky because you have to guess at distance. So it's not. I know that's a big disincentive. Anyway, so the game can fluctuate on who's ahead. You can have reversals. And anyway, so I don't know how to play it. I invented it. I don't know how to play it. So this guy killed this guy. So the game itself might be not very intellectual because it has guessing at distance and it has random board setups. The game itself is not intellectual, but I'll bet the first person who figures out how to play it is a smart person. Anyways.",
